          </param>
        </templateparamlist>
        <type>Marmot::Math::Vector6d</type>
        <definition>Marmot::Math::Vector6d Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Voigt::make3DVoigt</definition>
        <argsstring>(const Eigen::Matrix&lt; double, voigtSize, 1 &gt; &amp;Voigt)</argsstring>
        <name>make3DVoigt</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::ContinuumMechanics::Voigt::make3DVoigt</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const Eigen::Matrix&lt; double, voigtSize, 1 &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>Voigt</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Constructs a 3D Voigt vector from a lower-dimensional Voigt vector. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>voigtSize</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Dimension of the input Voigt vector (1, 3, or 6). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Voigt</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input Voigt vector of size <computeroutput>voigtSize</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>6-component 3D Voigt vector. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Considered cases:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>voigtSize = 1</computeroutput>: Returns a 3D vector with only <formula id="150">$\sigma_{11}$</formula> non-zero:     <formula id="151">\[\begin{bmatrix}
\sigma_{11} &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0 &amp; 0
\end{bmatrix}^T
\]</formula></para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>voigtSize = 3</computeroutput>: Returns a 3D Voigt vector by calling <computeroutput>planeVoigtToVoigt()</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>voigtSize = 6</computeroutput>: Returns the input vector unchanged. </para>
